  "methodology": [
    "Production measurements time actual bt_sync_folder MCP calls end to end, including tool/RPC overhead, both sequential server mirror legs, and filesystem work.",
    "Fresh full-copy repetitions use a different source path AND a fresh destination, preventing reuse of the server mirror.",
    "Direct tests use the existing installed RemoteSync and WorkerLink packages, one TCP hop, no TLS, after per-mode warmup. WebSocket setup is excluded; HTTP request setup is included. Receiver writes include page-cache writes, no fsync.",
    "SHA-256 verification is outside direct transfer timings. Production destination trees were verified after transfer.",
    "Large fixtures repeat a deterministic pseudorandom 1 MiB block; the 256 small files each contain the same deterministic pseudorandom 4096 bytes. Tests do not measure compression or a Git clone.",
    "The packed comparison uses an uncompressed tar, 1454080 bytes, for the same 256 files.",
    "Allocation figures are cumulative Julia allocations on the sender during the timed interval, not peak RSS.",
    "Server hostname resolved to home public IPv4 during this test. This does not establish how already-open worker connections are routed.",
    "Live WorkerLink pings reported approximately 20 ms for Desktop and Bosgame; ICMP mean RTT was 0.386 ms to Mini-Server, 0.440 ms to Bosgame, 0.585 ms to the home public IP.",
    "Actual production throughput varied. No production service, firewall, DNS, or transport setting was modified."
  ],
